                <sp:Bin_Description>
                    <sp:bin_profile_description>Christensen et al., 2017 describes the OTES instrument and detector calibrations in depth. In short, OTES collects 1350 ±3 double-sided interferogram samples. In order to have a consistent spectral sampling accounting for any sampling change over the life of the mission, the interferogram is filled with zeros to a uniform length of 1360 samples prior to performing the discrete Fourier transform. This number of samples, together with the measured laser wavelength of 0.849 μm resulting in a spectral sampling of 8.66 cm.</sp:bin_profile_description>
